From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: Keep Forza backing windows unmapped on wlroots.

Forza Horizon 5 renders its menu correctly, but its separate black backing
window covers the game on labwc. The backing window already has the
force_below_hack flag and _NET_WM_STATE_BELOW, but the compositor does not
honor the requested stacking. Unmapping that window reveals the rendered
menu; focusing the game maps the cover again.

Extend Paul Gofman's gamescope workaround from Wine commit 0dabe4b3e9c
to the "wlroots wm" X11 window manager. Apply the suppression in
window_set_wm_state using the latched force_below_hack flag, rather than
only when WindowPosChanged receives a specific insert_after window.
This also covers deferred state replay and subsequent focus updates.

Explicit Z order alone also matches the owned "Welcome to XBOX" login
dialog. Restrict the backing-window flag to disabled fullscreen tool popups
without WS_CHILD or WS_EX_APPWINDOW. Preserve the flag across focus and
minimize updates, but clear it if the window no longer has the backing
styles. The observed background has style 0x9c000000 and exstyle 0x80;
the login dialog has style 0x94c80000 and exstyle 0x308 and must not be
lowered or suppressed.

Keep the existing Forza 4/5/6 application list and Win32 visibility
unchanged. Do not change media decoding or native Wine-Wayland presentation.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/window.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1808,6 +1808,16 @@ static void window_set_wm_state( struct x11drv_win_data *data, UINT new_state, BOOL activate )
     UINT old_state = data->pending_state.wm_state;
     HWND foreground = NtUserGetForegroundWindow();
 
+    /* These compositors may stack Forza's black backing window above the game
+     * despite _NET_WM_STATE_BELOW. Keep it unmapped, including on state replay
+     * and focus changes, without hiding its Win32 window from the game. */
+    if (data->force_below_hack && (X11DRV_HasWindowManager( "steamcompmgr" ) ||
+                                 X11DRV_HasWindowManager( "wlroots wm" )))
+    {
+        new_state = WithdrawnState;
+        activate = FALSE;
+    }
+
     data->desired_state.wm_state = new_state;
     data->desired_state.activate = activate;
     if (data->state_locks) return; /* win32 state is being updated, delay the change */
@@ -3783,10 +3793,15 @@ void X11DRV_WindowPosChanged( HWND hwnd, HWND insert_after, HWND owner_hint, UINT swp_flags,
     if (use_force_below_hack())
     {
-        if (insert_after != HWND_BOTTOM && insert_after != HWND_NOTOPMOST && insert_after != HWND_TOP && insert_after != HWND_TOPMOST)
+        /* Login dialogs also use explicit Z order. Only the disabled fullscreen
+         * tool popup is a backing window; retain its flag across focus changes. */
+        if ((new_style & (WS_POPUP | WS_DISABLED | WS_CHILD)) != (WS_POPUP | WS_DISABLED) ||
+            (ex_style & (WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW | WS_EX_APPWINDOW)) != WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW)
+            data->force_below_hack = 0;
+        else if (fullscreen && insert_after != HWND_BOTTOM && insert_after != HWND_NOTOPMOST &&
+                 insert_after != HWND_TOP && insert_after != HWND_TOPMOST)
         {
             WARN( "%p/%#lx setting force_below_hack.\n", hwnd, data->whole_window );
             data->force_below_hack = 1;
-            if (X11DRV_HasWindowManager( "steamcompmgr" )) new_style &= ~WS_VISIBLE;
         }
     }
 
